cked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":37,"created_at":"2020-12-17T09:35:16Z","updated_at":"2023-06-29T14:10:48Z","closed_at":"2023-06-29T14:10:47Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nWhen calling the deleteAll function to delete all the entities. It's expected to delete also the child entities if it has been configured to use cascade ALL or REMOVE:\r\n\r\n```java\r\n@Entity(name = \"application\")\r\npublic class ApplicationEntity extends PanacheEntity {\r\n    // ...\r\n\r\n    @OneToMany(mappedBy = \"application\", cascade = CascadeType.ALL, orphanRemoval = true, fetch = FetchType.EAGER)\r\n    public List<ServiceEntity> services = new ArrayList<>();\r\n```\r\n\r\nDelete all method usage:\r\n\r\n```java\r\nApplicationEntity.deleteAll();\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis works fine if we delete the entity individually:\r\n\r\n```java\r\nApplicationEntity.findById(actualEntityId).delete();\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nDelete one item and delete all should behave the same, so both methods should delete the child entities if cascade is properly configured.\r\n\r\n**Actual behavior**\r\nDeleteAll method is not deleting child entities even though the cascade is properly configured.\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nYou can run [this test](https://github.com/Sgitario/beefy-scenarios/blob/916b397def22313707a439d892ecbd3a2e7bd6d7/011-quarkus-panache-rest-flyway/src/test/java/io/quarkus/qe/ApplicationEntityTest.java#L29) as a reproducer. \r\nThe test is failing and it should pass.\r\n\r\n**Environment (please complete the following information):**\r\n - GraalVM version (if different from Java): \r\n - Quarkus version or git rev: 1.10.3.Final\r\n - Build tool (ie. output of `mvnw --version` or `gradlew --version`): \r\n"